      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "The node lands multiple resolutions (module buried, machine departs, Pip urinates on the patch, Wes names it \u0027Lord Long Legs\u0027) and then closes on \u0027I\u0027ll walk,\u0027 which reads as a hopeful/settled character beat rather than a quiet gesture that adds cost or dread; the final exchange is almost warm/whimsical, undercutting the \u0027holding the cost\u0027 effect.",
      "Fix": "Cut or dampen the naming exchange and end instead on a single unresolved image (e.g., the sealed asphalt scar, or Wes\u0027s silence at the horizon) that carries unease about what the buried module means and what \u0027this city/corridor\u0027 will do next, without supplying an origin-story punchline like the dog\u0027s territorial joke."
